+/* NEUTRON: MediaPlayer plays through IMFMediaEngine.
+ *
+ * Every member used to be a stub, so an app could create a player but never play anything with
+ * it. Lightroom Classic's video toolkit plays its in-app help videos (the Assisted Culling tip in
+ * the Import dialog) as MediaSource -> MediaPlaybackItem -> MediaPlayer in frame server mode,
+ * copying each frame into its own D3D11 surface with CopyFrameToVideoSurface.
+ *
+ * Threading. The media engine calls IMFMediaEngineNotify with its own lock held, on its worker
+ * threads and sometimes on the caller's thread. So the notify callback never runs app code: it
+ * records state and queues an event. A worker thread per player delivers queued events in order
+ * and runs the frame server pump (OnVideoStreamTick -> VideoFrameAvailable). The engine callback
+ * never takes the player's lock, so an app thread holding it while calling into the engine cannot
+ * deadlock against an engine thread. */
